courses.topical_outline:
Through readings, experiential projects, and class discussions, students gain understanding of a particular topic in the field of art museum education. Emphasis is placed on issues that are relative to current art museum education practice. This course addresses topics in art museum education. The specific topic of the course will vary from year to year, and may cover topics such as (but not limited to): 
- museum education history
- theoretical underpinnings of museum education practice
- contemporary issues in the field, such as: 
decolonizing museum practice;  
diversity, equity, inclusion, and accessibility in museum education gallery teaching and programs; 
community engagement and outreach; 
and creative and multi-modal approaches to museum education. A final paper or project allows students the opportunity to relate selected readings and class activities to an area of personal interest.

